  "sub_0_5s_coverage_gap_note": "Uniform candidates are sampled at ~2fps (500ms native gap). Any on-screen text/URL/code with a visible duration under ~0.5s can fall entirely between two uniform samples. Scene-change and text-region-change candidates partially mitigate this by catching hard cuts and lower-third content changes, but this remains a documented coverage gap for very short on-screen text.",
